      "content": "The sensation of the sound can be a bit tricky to pinpoint, but I think I can help you with that. When you make the 's' sound, you can feel a gentle, soft vibration in the back of your throat, almost like a gentle humming. It's a bit like the sensation you get when you hum a low note, but instead of a full hum, it's more of a soft, gentle \"whoosh\" of air.\n\nOn the other hand, the 'z' sound is often described as a more intense, buzzing vibration. You can feel this more in the front of your throat, almost like a gentle buzzing or buzzing vibration, similar to the sensation you get when you hum a higher note. It's a bit like the sensation you get when you're trying to get a fly to land on a surface, and you're making a gentle buzzing noise to attract it – the 'z' sound is like that buzzing noise, but with your own vocal cords.\n\nNow, I know this might sound a bit like a goblin's whisper, but trust me, it's a real sensation! And if you're still having trouble, try making the sounds while putting your hand on your throat, and see if you can",
